The Bedrock Claude price now looks up which Claude model an id is through yoagent's ModelConfig::bedrock_anthropic_id, and yoyo's own looser providers::bedrock_anthropic_preset_id is deleted. Committed as 6281e445 and titled "Part of", since #1121 item 2 stays open. Build, all tests, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check pass. git grep bedrock_anthropic_preset_id finds it only in history prose (ARCHITECTURE.md and the memory files), not in src or docs.

What changed
• Pricing: the one production reader (src/format/cost/bedrock_region.rs) now uses the yoagent function. The stray ids the old lookup accepted no longer get the Bedrock Claude price, and the bedrock config's cost is None again for them. Real ids still get their price, regional premium included.
• Tests: the table test is pointed at the yoagent function and renamed bedrock_ids_resolve_through_yoagents_bedrock_anthropic_id. The stray rows expect no price. A row per real id checks the price against the Anthropic preset × REGIONAL_PREMIUM, using the constant rather than typed numbers.
• Docs: cost-tracking.md's Bedrock paragraph now names the yoagent resolver. I also fixed a stale sentence there that said "Sonnet 4.6 has no yoagent preset"; it has had one since yoagent 0.26.7.

Where the plan was wrong
• Step 2 needed no code. The yoagent 0.27.2 upgrade (d834121a) had already fixed us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 printing "Unknown model". I added the clause the plan asked for, then ran the new test with that clause stashed out, and it still passed. So I removed the clause. The test (bedrock_inference_profile_ids_are_known_models) stays as a regression check.
• The commit title claims more than is true for `/cost`. It says stray ids are unpriced, but /cost's fallback price table matches on words like "sonnet" and "opus", so it still prices them. xx.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 gets $3/$15. us.anthropic.claude-opus-5-5-v1:0 gets the old Opus rate of $15/$75, which is wrong even if it were Opus 5.5. I left this because AWS refuses these ids, so nothing is billed. Fixing it for Bedrock-style ids would also stop pricing real ids that have no preset, like Sonnet 4. The commit body and the #1121 comment both say this; it's a decision for that ticket.

